        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f2de49ac-cb6c-5d74-93a4-da158fe866b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Fallada, John Buchan\n- Works: Everyone Dies Alone, Every Man Dies Alone\n- Roles: Writer, Novelist, Historian, Politician, Governor General of Canada\n- Places: Germany, Canada, West Germany\n\nFacts:\n- John Buchan was born on 26 August 1875 and was a Scottish novelist, historian, and Unionist politician.\n- Hans Fallada, born Rudolf Wilhelm Friedrich Ditzen on 21 July 1893, was a German writer of the first half of the 20th century.\n- John Buchan served as Governor General of Canada and was the 15th officeholder since Canadian Confederation.\n- John Buchan, 1st Baron Tweedsmuir, died on 11 February 1940.\n- Hans Fallada died on 5 February 1947.\n- The film Everyone Dies Alone was produced and released in West Germany in 1975.\n- Everyone Dies Alone is the original-title German film Jeder stirbt für sich allein.\n- Everyone Dies Alone was adapted from the Hans Fallada novel Every Man Dies Alone.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
